ow it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each condition:\n\n- We're given that $y=-4$ and $y=-1$ are equilibrium points. We represent this on the phase line by drawing two distinct points at these locations.\n\n- We're given that $y=-1$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-1$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=-4$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-4$ (already drawn by the above property) and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\nTherefore, our phase line is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/8a5f3a5965878cba364ee0e96af77bea41d53e6b2bd440340d72215e30db3a83.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98709/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "680a42fd-9b70-5fb2-916c-d10b71b11d82"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-96558"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/9230d847daa518edfaad43f6552a48c2b3cac9523a1e9ecad8624851080e00ea.png)\n\nA particular autonomous differential equation has the phase line shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=-1$ is a source\n- $y=2$ is a sink\n- $y=2$ is a node" :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=-1$ points upward, and the arrow just below it points downward. In other words, both arrows point *away* from  $y=-1.$ This means that $y=-1$ is a source.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=2$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points upward. In other words, both arrows point *toward* the point $y=2.$This means that $y=2$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-98753"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/97d1a6a7f167b29a12e2f586067f6d7fa3cb5afec0be0ae854512cfe5c968d42.png)\n\nConsider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=2$ is a node.\n- $y=2$ is a source.\n- $y=-4$ is a sink." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/7ad82b4ff48bbf69efccf5a822c7013929224a1a6e6e63e1948ea9ea95dcc858.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=2$ is a source.\n\n- Statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-4$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339709/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3f7fa5ba-613a-531a-8c82-c7388aa1a325" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339709/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "666aaf3b-15f4-5312-8d0a-a9553c537164" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339709/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "496a9117-9d71-54eb-a398-3e59f6f02cbb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339709/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "95aa0559-9481-5907-b392-8993f99520e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339709/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "23cf78f2-86fc-5860-886b-6e7d97bdaa47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339709/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa9c192-a00