inting arrow just below $y=-2$ and a downward-pointing arrow just above it.\n\n- We're given that $y=3$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just below $y=3$ (already drawn by the above property) and an upward-pointing arrow just above it.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/3d2eec912d188cd569c4f87558a148c808ee2c815eeca7289103f11465d98859.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/d11dbd5ae88f62511de12bf4745fc055d59f5ef20de6125685217d87e5e08b17.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-2$ and $y=3.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-2$ appear to converge toward this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=3$ appear to diverge away from this line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98785/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58b04cc-da5e-5c51-a583-0663d783c697"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98785"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98814/selection/9eabdf71164df02f069d84ceced46984543b3b3c908dd7bada0f3da543db21db" :answer/id #uuid "67294cf7-c3ab-50fe-bd6b-59c00c411069" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/06a3d9118f9e3c09f374760a6e8209b33c9458e4d4b476c56fae3c57f2ca3fbe.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98814/selection/8291b351b57658636dbd76d68cdce93a338ed3a301f998088a2a927e78111146" :answer/id #uuid "92b17b9a-4748-516f-8b99-ba0db609cbde" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/fd79ddf3d04b18f0b9740aa3a03ed